# Lists where two PRs' added lines are always both right, merged by keeping both sides' lines
# (DEC-2600 item 6). `merge=union` applies only to merges git runs locally (`git merge main` in a
# lane's checkout); GitHub's web merge and "Update branch" ignore it. The checks still read every
# merged line: `cargo xtask deps` refuses a dependency row kept twice, `cargo xtask layers` parses
# layers.toml (a key kept twice fails to parse) and checks CODEOWNERS' crate lines are sorted.
/docs/dependencies.md merge=union
/CODEOWNERS merge=union
/xtask/layers.toml merge=union
